  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Emergency Cash Assistance to vulnerable Lebanese and Syrian refugee families in border areas affected by the tensions in the South</narrative>
  </title>
  <description type="1">
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The main objective of this project is to provide multi-purpose cash transfers for food and other necessities to Syrian refugees and Lebanese nationals affected by the cross-border conflict in South Lebanon in the Sour, Marjaayoun, Bint Jbeil and Hasbaya districts, South and Nabatiyeh governates. Under the Multi-Purpose Cash sector, this project will provide humanitarian assistance to 39,088 people, including 10,487 women, 19,104 children, and 1,489 persons with disabilities.</narrative>
  </description>
